1597..1674 Comment "/// The three laws together. Associativity\'s inner `ext(m, k)` is an instance"
1675..1742 Comment "/// of its own left side and of both unit laws\', and its right side"
1743..1810 Comment "/// substitutes `k` under `bind x .`: each pair is found by pattern"
1811..1870 Comment "/// unification, and its two reducts normalize to one term."
